<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karad is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satara">Satara</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, at the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> and Koyna rivers. An ancient settlement with early Buddhist rock-cut caves nearby, it lay in the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silahara-dynasty">Silahara dynasty</a> of Kolhapur, who arose in the region in the 10th century. It is now a regional centre of trade and education.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karad.jpg" alt="Karad" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Basargimahesh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IMG_Karad2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
